open — needs a human at a real browser:
Click one Download → .csv and one Methods → Copy, and confirm a file lands / the
clipboard fills. Both were wired and checked structurally (every format resolves
to a live blob URL with the right filename, or to a function that exists), but
neither final step could be exercised: Chrome refuses automatic downloads from
the dev origin after a handful of saves, and the clipboard write needs a genuine
user gesture. If Copy fails it falls back to showing the text selected in the
output pane, so nothing is lost either way.

open — decision, not a bug:
"Symbols not found" and "Pick human cell line" line up when the page loads, but
entering adapter sequences shows the oligo preview and pushes the third column
down ~70px. "Load test data" fills the adapters, so the demo path shows the
shift. The two columns hold independently variable content and cannot stay
locked in every state. Reserving the space permanently would fix it at the cost
of a visible gap in the default view — left as is until someone decides.

open — other repo:
Correlate has the same cropped-logo bug on a phone (fixed-width logo, no
`max-width` rule anywhere). Fix is `header img { max-width: 100%; height: auto }`
plus letting the header nav wrap. Worth also sweeping that app for horizontal
overflow at 390px — the same sweep here found two more real overflows in a modal
that eyeballing had missed.

